<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $22.80 bln on Sept 20.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $22.80 bln on Sept 20.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $22.80 billion on September 20, 1996, from $22.75 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>	 FOREIGN EXCHANGE RESERVES (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Sept 20     Sept 13     Sept 22</p>
<p>					    1996	  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     18,288	18,143	 19,102</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,455	 4,455	  4,413</p>
<p>    SDRs				    57	   155	     49</p>
<p>    Total			     22,800	22,753	 23,564</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
